    "body": "## What does this PR do?\n\nPreserve cumulative FLOP metadata when saving a training checkpoint. The finalizer currently overwrites `TrainState`'s float64 counter with float32: for example, 16,777,217 becomes 16,777,216 before the train-state sidecar is saved and later restored on resume.\n\nUse float64 in that finalizer, matching `TrainState.state_dict()` and MCore's train-state serialization from NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#7516. The regression extends the existing global-save test over both RNG-save settings, a small value, the float32 precision boundary, and a value above the int64 range. Expected precision is float64, not arbitrary integer precision.\n\n## Supported path and ownership\n\nPublic recipe training -> `save_checkpoint_and_time` -> checkpoint manager -> `save_checkpoint` -> `train_state_finalize_fn` -> `train_state.pt` and latest-state metadata -> resume. Bridge owns this callback; updating the MCore pin does not replace it. Only the callback dtype and its regression test change.\n\nRecorded Bridge base: `7feb75ef9410bcda80427499ce4ab44907043b61`.\nPinned MCore: `e0c5e18673bf4d4fd89cf87c4f1afbe521fe297f`.\nUpstream MCore main inspected: `e30d863a6d82a3c45f2d71355dc73fbf5610967b`.\n\nBoth-repository, all-state duplicate searches covered the counter/finalizer symbols, float64 checkpoint metadata and FLOP precision. Core PR 6807 changes upstream sidecar handling; Bridge PR 6227 changes runtime FLOP calculation, PR 3506 safe loading, PR 2817 EMA callbacks, and issue 3267 iteration snapshot ordering. They do not repair this dtype overwrite.\n\n## Validation\n\nIdentical command before and after the production change:\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/training/test_checkpointing.py -k save_checkpoint_global -q -p no:cacheprovider\n```\n\n- Before: unchanged production plus test only; exit 1, six cases fail `torch.float32 == torch.float64`. The 16,777,217 case contains 16,777,216.\n- After: exit 0, six passed.\n\nAdjacent validation:\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/training/test_checkpointing.py tests/unit_tests/training/test_state.py -k 'TestSaveCheckpoint or TestTrainState' -q -p no:cacheprovider\nuv run pre-commit run --all-files\n```\n\nAdjacent tests: exit 0, 30 passed and one skipped. All-files hooks: exit 0, no modifications. Fresh read-only review found no blocking issue.\n\nTests use native Bridge imports and the exact pinned Core source on CPU; the existing unit fixture mocks checkpoint I/O and distributed calls. No multi-rank training-resume or performance result is claimed.\n\n`uv run mypy --strict src/megatron/bridge/training/checkpointing.py tests/unit_tests/training/test_checkpointing.py` exits 2 with the same mypy 2.2.0 internal error on the unchanged base and patched source. No type-check pass is claimed.\n",
